🛒CODING ASSIGNMENT

End-to-end test automation suite for the **SimplCommerce Demo Store** using **Playwright (JavaScript)**.

This project contains a small set of smoke/regression tests focused on the main ecommerce flow:
- Add to cart
- Remove from cart
- Update product quantity
- Checkout with valid details
- Checkout with missing/invalid details

---

## Tech Stack

- **Playwright**
- **JavaScript (Node.js)**
- **dotenv** (environment variables)

---

## Requirements

- **Node.js 18+**
- npm

---

## Installation

Clone the repository and install dependencies:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Spidey44/MN-Coding-Exercise---Automate-demo.simplcommerce-with-Playwright.git
cd MN-Coding-Exercise---Automate-demo.simplcommerce-with-Playwright
npm install
```

---

## Install Playwright browsers:
```bash
npx playwright install
```

---

## Environment Variables (.env)
Create a .env file in the root of the project:
```bash
BASE_URL=https://example.com
EMAIL_USER=your-email@example.com
PASS_USER=your-password
```

Example:

```bash
BASE_URL=https://demo.simplcommerce.com
EMAIL_USER=janedoe@test.com
PASS_USER=Test123!
```
These credentials are used for login before checkout tests.

---

## Running Tests

Run all tests:
```bash
npx playwright test
```

Run in headed mode (browser visible):
```bash
npx playwright test --headed
```

Run a single test file:
```bash
npx playwright test tests/cart-add.spec.js
```

Run a specific test by name:
```bash
npx playwright test -g "Adding a product to the cart"
```

---

## Test Report
After execution, open the HTML report:

```bash
npx playwright show-report
```

## 🧪 Test Suite Overview
The following tests are included as required examples:

### ✅ Cart
- TC_CART_001 - Adding a product to the cart
- TC_CART_002 - Removing a product from the cart
- TC_CART_003 - Updating product quantity

### ✅ Checkout
- TC_CHECK_001 - Proceeding to checkout with valid details
- TC_CHECK_010 - Attempting checkout with missing/invalid details (no address / invalid payment)

## 🔁 Data-Driven Tests
Some tests are implemented using a simple data-driven approach.
Example structure:

```js
const cases = [
  { name: "iPhone 6s 16GB", url: "/iphone-6s-16gb", addClicks: 2 },
  { name: "Dell XPS 15 9550", url: "/dell-xps-15-9550", addClicks: 1 },
  ...
];

for (const c of cases) {
  test(`[Product] Updating product quantity - ${c.name}`, async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto(c.url);
    // ...
  });
}
```

** This makes it easy to scale test coverage by simply adding new products/cases without duplicating logic.**

## 🎯 Selector Strategy
The test suite prioritizes readable selectors such as:
- getByText(...) (UI-visible strings)
- getByRole(...) (recommended by Playwright for stable interactive elements)

Example:
```js
const addCartBtn = page.getByRole("button", { name: "Add to cart" });
await addCartBtn.click();
```

